# What `docker build -f backend/Dockerfile .` can see.
#
# An allow-list. The context has to be the repo root (the API serves /img from
# reference/), and the root also holds .env with a real TMDB token, so nothing is
# sent unless it is named below. It also keeps the context around 1.6 MB instead of
# including backend/target and frontend/node_modules.
#
# A new build input has to be added here. That fails loudly at build time.
*

# Manifests, copied separately so the dependency layer keys on them alone.
!backend/Cargo.toml
!backend/Cargo.lock

!backend/src

# The export's posters and avatars. Only img/ — the rest of reference/ is mockups.
!reference/cine-journal/img

# Already excluded by `*`. Listed so a future `!` line doesn't undo it by accident.
.env
.env.*
**/*.db
**/*.db-wal
**/*.db-shm
